{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/808246-help-me-break-balance-a-custom-demon-form-ability","id":808246,"title":"Help me break/balance a custom demon form ability","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T14:45:54-08:00","id":808246,"title":"Help me break/balance a custom demon form ability","content":"So, one of the players in my current Demon game didn't quite manage to find a 4th Modification for his Demon form that suited what he had in mind for his demon. We spent some time trying to come up with a custom Modification that could work for his character, and this is what he came up with in the end. We only have the basics so far, but I figured I should throw it up here to see how you feel about it,<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Replicator</b><br /> The demon can store designs of up to 3(?) small items (about 4*4 inches / 10*10 cm or somewhere around there). He can spend 1 Aether and a standard action to create one of these items from his body. The items replicated are extensions of his demonic form, so a phone attached to his arm could be created, but a grenade cannot be replicated and then thrown at his enemies. Gadgets and other supernatural items cannot be stored or replicated with this Modification.<br /> <br /> Initially, I was worried that he would begin just creating loads of explosives or something to that effect, but with the added limit that the replicated objects are attached to his body this seems to be solved. He does have the Detachable Limbs technology however, which increases the risk for this to be broken slightly more.<br /> <br /> So, how balanced or unbalanced would you say this Modification would be? I'm still a bit worried that it intrudes on In my pocket / Deep Pockets, as well as the Shielded Compartment Technology from Flowers of Hell. One possible disadvantage that could be added (that I've thought of) would be that storing designs for this Modification would take quite some time and destroy the original item, as well as limit the duration of replicated items (although I'm not quite sure how necessary that would be since they're bound to his demonic form.<br /> <br /> Basically, would this break the game, or would it be just fine? How would you go about making it better/worse if you think that's needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/586-gurrgel","name":"Gurrgel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:02:53-08:00","id":808260,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem I can see is that this\u2026 isn't really a Modification, conceptually speaking. It's basically a version of the Nanobot Composition Process that can make more sophisticated objects; Modifications largely enhance or alter existing humanlike capabilities.<br /> <br /> What is he going for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:51:00-08:00","id":808296,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the Embed <i>In My Pocket</i> accomplish all these things, with no Aether cost, no chance of compromise and a trivially simple roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:27:04-08:00","id":808725,"title":"","content":"Tried to get the OP written before I went to bed but perhaps I should've spent some more time on it. Thanks for your replies anyway, I've tried to add some further details below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/808246-help-me-break-balance-a-custom-demon-form-ability?p=808296#post808296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't the Embed <i>In My Pocket</i> accomplish all these things, with no Aether cost, no chance of compromise and a trivially simple roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's definitely part of my worries, to some extent I don't mind a modification being a slightly worse version of an Embed, but in this case they might be a bit too close to each other, and that's definitely one of my problems with it that I mentioned to my player.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/808246-help-me-break-balance-a-custom-demon-form-ability?p=808260#post808260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem I can see is that this\u2026 isn't really a Modification, conceptually speaking. It's basically a version of the Nanobot Composition Process that can make more sophisticated objects; Modifications largely enhance or alter existing humanlike capabilities.<br /> <br /> What is he going for?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely related to Nanobot Composition, I guess I'll have to go into the background behind all of this a bit more. With me and my group not having English as our native tongue, we did not know that Simple Tools / Simple Machines (whichever phrase Nanobot Composition uses) was an established concept with a clear definition, and since something that's simple today is quite a bit more advanced than what it was back when the expression was established, Nanobot Composition was a bit over the top which, when combined with Detachable Limbs, allowed him to send off his limbs reconfigured into whatever was needed to infiltrate pretty much anything (especially since they could reconfigure their form on the go), with vision from cameras or such created from Nanobot Composition thanks to being what we (incorrectly) thought was a simple machine...<br /> <br /> Since I felt this ruined the fun for much of the group (definitely for other players, but partially for the player in question as well due to the low risk, high reward playstyle), I looked into Nanobot Composition which is when I found out what Simple Tools actually means. <br /> <br /> So, to some extent he's definitely trying to recreate the former glory of the much more powerful version of Nanobot Composition that we used previously. To some extent I could be fine with this, since my new understanding of the actual limits of Nanobot his modes of transportation are much more limited now than when we thought that he could shapeshift the limbs he'd sent off to whatever he needed for the situation. I am however still a bit worried that this promotes the type of low risk gameplay that's not too much fun for anyone (in my opinion). I'm not trying to crush his dreams, but at the same time, I much prefer when my players find cool ways to solve problems, rather than him just sending in a part of his body to spy without any real risk since he can just destroy it and grow a new limb from his body if it faces any real danger.<br /> <br /> I guess that mostly answers you final question about what he's going for, but I figured I should start with the background for all of this. <br /> <br /> I am aware about the descriptions regarding what different Demonic Form Abilities are meant to do / give you, but since those descriptions only loosely (if at all) apply to the abilities in the books to begin with, I'm not sure how strict I can be about that for his custom power. Abilities like Detachable Limbs / EMP Field / Nauseating Musk don't really fit the written description of Modifications, Likewise you have Electrical Sight / Component Indicators / Advanced Optics under Modifications, but Aura Sight is a Technology despite doing a very similar thing.<br /> <br /> This particular power may not be quite salvageable as a Modification (I'm probably leaning in that direction myself), I'd just prefer if I could avoid crushing the player's ideas if possible. At least now you should have all the details that I've got available. Do you feel a power like this one (or some version of it) would be better suited as a Technology? I realise it has some overlap with Nanobot Composition still, but I feel like Nanobot Composition's other advantages more than make up for the parts &quot;lost&quot; to this modification. This power may be too powerful to exist all together, and that's definitely a possible problem, but I'm not really worried about it overlapping too much with the Process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/586-gurrgel","name":"Gurrgel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}